{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "godunov_upwind_D1_2d_paraboloid_mms",
    "description": "Method-of-manufactured-solutions order-of-accuracy driver for the per-axis rules grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_upwind_D1x_extrapolate_bc and godunov_upwind_D1y_extrapolate_bc (NCAR fire_behavior's classical Godunov option, fire_upwinding = 4: diff2 = max(D-,0) - min(D+,0) per axis) with the linear-extrapolation halo closure. The norm is spelled as the compound sqrt((D(u,x))^2 + (D(u,y))^2) but NO compound rule is imported, so the two inner D's lower per axis to Gx = max(D-x u, 0) - min(D+x u, 0) and Gy likewise, and the norm evaluated is sqrt(Gx^2 + Gy^2) = sqrt(max(D-x,0)^2 + min(D+x,0)^2 - 2 max(D-x,0) min(D+x,0) + ...) -- the Rouy-Tourin Hamiltonian plus a non-negative cross term that vanishes on monotone data; both are first-order consistent with |grad u|. Forced-steady eikonal u_t = S (|grad g| - sqrt(Gx^2 + Gy^2)) with the smooth manufactured paraboloid g = (x-1/2)^2 + (y-1/2)^2 - 0.09 (zero level set: the circle r = 0.3) and forcing |grad g| = 2 r; g is exact for all t and the discrete imbalance is the first-order truncation, so the L2 error is O(h) (expected order 1). The signed distance r - 0.3 is deliberately NOT used: its convex centre kink is not a steady viscosity solution and fills in (see problems/levelset_weno5_eno1_2d_paraboloid_mms.esm). Wall cells: g increases toward every wall, so the guarded extrapolation ghost is the plain linear one and the wall error is the same first-order one-sided truncation as the interior. The reference's small L2 norm (~0.09) inflates the RELATIVE L2 error about tenfold; the cap is set from the measured value. Geometry: x0 = y0 = 0, dx = 1/NX, dy = 1/NY; coordinates inline from literals and NX, NY. Per-resolution errors in tests/conformance/convergence/godunov_upwind_D1_2d_paraboloid_mms/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "equation:hamilton_jacobi",
      "mms",
      "level_set"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Rouy, E., & Tourin, A. (1992). A viscosity solutions approach to shape-from-shading. SIAM J. Numer. Anal. 29, 867-884.",
        "doi": "10.1137/0729053"
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NX": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 64,
      "description": "Cells along x (default resolution of the inline test; rebound by the convergence runner)."
    },
    "NY": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 64,
      "description": "Cells along y."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "GodunovUpwindD1ParaboloidMMS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_upwind_D1x_extrapolate_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NX": "NX",
            "NY": "NY"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_upwind_D1y_extrapolate_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NX": "NX",
            "NY": "NY"
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "Level-set field integrated under the forced eikonal u_t = S (|grad g| - sqrt(Gx^2 + Gy^2)) with Gx, Gy the per-axis Godunov-upwind quantities; starts at and stays near the paraboloid g = r^2 - 0.09."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Non-negative Hamilton-Jacobi front speed."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left x domain edge (grid free name)."
        },
        "y0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Bottom y domain edge (grid free name)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "x-spacing 1/NX: the grid dx free name, NX substituted at load (esm-spec 9.7.6)."
        },
        "dy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "y-spacing 1/NY: the grid dy free name, NY substituted at load."
        },
        "forcing": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "The manufactured |grad g| = 2 r (coordinates spelled inline)."
